From: vmapp <vmapp@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] app: let the desktop app's Go packages build on linux

The desktop app (app/ui, app/store, app/server, app/tools, ...) is tagged `windows || darwin`, because its only front ends are the macOS
and Windows apps. None of those packages needs the desktop (no cgo UI, no webview): they are a web server, a SQLite store and a
supervisor of `ollama serve`. Widening the tag to linux makes them build, so that a headless front end (apps/ollama-desktop/backend/
vmapp-ui) can run the app's real Go backend in a Linux VM. The only code that has to be added is the one function of the macOS
and Windows updater that app/ui calls.

